performance-4.lyrics_transcript:
Be merciful, be gracious; spare him, Lord.
Be merciful, be gracious; Lord, deliver him.
From the sins that are past,
From thy drown and Thine ire;
From the perils of dying;
From any complying
With sin, or denying
His God, or relying
On self, at the last;
From the nethermost fire;
From all that is evil;
From power of the devil;
Thy servant deliver,
For once and for ever.
By Thy birth, and by Thy Cross,
Rescue him from endless loss;
By Thy death and burial,
Save him from a final fall;
By Thy rising from the tomb,
By Thy mounting up above,
By the Spirit's gracious love,
Save him in the day of doom.

performance_3.lyrics_transcript:
Like silver lamps in a distant shrine
    The stars are sparkling bright;
    The bells of the city of God ring out,
    For the Son of Mary was born to-night;
    The gloom is past, and the morn at last
    Is coming with orient light.

    Never fell melodies half so sweet
    As those which are filling the skies;
    And never a palace shone half so fair
    As the manger bed where our Saviour lies;
    No night in the year is half so dear
    As this which has ended our sighs.

    Now a new power has come on earth,
    A match for the armies of Hell;
    A Child is born who shall conquer the foe,
    And all the spirits of wickedness quell;
    For Mary's Son is the Mighty One
    Whom the prophets of God foretell.

    The stars of heaven still shine as at first
    They gleamed on this wonderful night
    The bells of the city of God peal out,
    And the Angels' song still rings in the height;
    And love still burns where the Godhead burns,
    Hid in Flesh from our daily sight.

    Faith sees no longer the stable floor,
    The pavement of sapphire is there;
    The bright stream of Heaven streams out to the world,
    And Angels of God are crowding the air;
    And Heaven and earth, through the spotless birth,
    Are at peace on this night so fair.

performance_2.lyrics_transcript:
THE evening approaches and the autumnal breeze is blowing;
Hoarfrost encircles the firs;
O crosier and book and monks prayer;
We must all leave here (go away from here).

The native country is getting dark, dusky and cold;
The holy springs are running turbidly.
Already the axe is flashing to fell thee
Thou green forest, round which the gods are hovering.

And we depart silently, a beaten army;
Extinguished are our stars;
O Iceland, icy rock of the sea,
Rise up in mighty distance!

Rise up and receive our equipped race!
The old gods, the old right,
The old Normans
Upon rostrate ships come swimming.

Where the volcano is blazing embers are falling,
Stormy waves surround the shores with foam;
Upon thee, thou defying extremity of the world
We will dream away the winter night.

performance_23.lyrics_transcript:
Ashes our temple soon will be;
Frithjof from his home must flee!
Happy he who departs not forever!

performance_5.lyrics_transcript:
Tho' long years have passed away,
    And joyous summer left me;
Tho' autumn sings her plaintive lay,
    Yet art thou still dear to me.

Tho' far away, thy voice is ever near to me;
Absence but makes thee dearer to me;
No time can change my love for thee.

performance_6.lyrics_transcript:
Thou the tempest unchianest;
Thy storms Thy word obey;
The vast sea Thou restrained;
Be our shield, Lord today!

performance_5.lyrics_transcript:
Oh, turn away, my son, and go not there!
Avoid this stranger's seductive devices;
Heed not her voice, though softly it entices;
Of the serpent's deadly fang beware!

Oh, turn away, my son, and go not there!
Avoid this stranger's seductive devices;
Heed not her voice, though softly it entices;
Of the serpent's deadly fang beware!

performance_7.lyrics_transcript:
Sweet is the lily's perfumed breath;
Swetter far are my warm caresses;
There awaits thee, Love, joy that blesses
And all that bliss awakeneth!
Open thine arms, my brave defender!
Let me fly to thy sheltering breast;
There on thy heart I will sweetly rest,
Filling my soul with rapture tender,
Come, O come!

performance_17.lyrics_transcript:
I have climbed o'er the cheerless
Mountain-peaks to thy side;
'Mid dangers I was fearless;
Dagon served as my guide!

performance_18.lyrics_transcript:
I greet you, worthy master;
A welcome face you show,
Honored e'er as priest and pastor!

performance_22.lyrics_transcript:
Although his brothers warn him,
And he hears what they say,
They all coldly scorn him
Because he loves astray;
Yet still, in spite of reason,
He struggles all in vain;
I fear from him no treason,
For his heart I retain!
'Tis in vain he defies me,
Though so mighty in his arms;
Not a wish he denies me;
He melts before my charms.

performance_35.lyrics_transcript:
Then I go, lest he find me belated;
But soon by secret paths I bring the
avenging band;
Now the fate of thy land
Is lodged within thy hand.
Unveil his secret heart,
And rob him of his treasure;
Make him tell where resides
That force which none can measure.
(Exit.)

performance_40.lyrics_transcript:
Ah! cease that wild discourse;
At thy words all my soul
Is darkened with remorse.
